From e122ba4ba09807d1c0af0c668f628e1f7e9fe137 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Stoyan <andrey.stoyan.csam@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 14:11:45 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat(chexc): annotate stdx url and serialization; macros
 declare what they raise

stdx.encoding.url: every public entry point that parses -- 'URL.parse', the constructing 'init',
'resolveURL', the 'replace' overloads, 'decode'/'decodeComponent', the 'query' and 'queryForm'
accessors, 'Form(queryComponent:)' -- declares 'UrlSyntaxException'. 19 diagnostics to none.

stdx.serialization: 'Serializable.deserialize' declares 'DataModelException', which is what every
one of its nineteen implementations already throws, and 'serialize' declares it too because the
'HashMap' implementation raises it for a non-String key. Only the five implementations that
forward through the interface restate it; the rest narrow to nothing, which coverage allows. Two
judgment calls, both recorded: 'Rune.deserialize' raised a bare 'Exception' for "not a single
Rune" and now raises 'DataModelException' like every other mismatch in the file, since an
implementation may narrow the interface's list but never widen it.

The macros of stdx.actors and stdx.plugin declare the exception they raise while expanding, which
the compiler now accepts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
